  "content": {
    "id": "v2-50a09-p41-practice-topup-slot-1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Arrange these fractions in ascending order.\n$1\\frac{5}{6},\\ \\frac{9}{4},\\ 2\\frac{1}{3},\\ \\frac{11}{4},\\ 2\\frac{1}{2}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1\\frac{5}{6},\\ \\frac{9}{4},\\ 2\\frac{1}{3},\\ 2\\frac{1}{2},\\ \\frac{11}{4}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1\\frac{5}{6}&=\\frac{11}{6}=\\frac{22}{12}\\\\\\frac{9}{4}&=\\frac{27}{12}\\\\2\\frac{1}{3}&=\\frac{7}{3}=\\frac{28}{12}\\\\\\frac{11}{4}&=\\frac{33}{12}\\\\2\\frac{1}{2}&=\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{30}{12}\\end{align*}$$\nThe LCD is $12$. Since $22<27<28<30<33$, the ascending order is $1\\frac{5}{6},\\ \\frac{9}{4},\\ 2\\frac{1}{3},\\ 2\\frac{1}{2},\\ \\frac{11}{4}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
